  <prompt>Owner 2026-11-25: "Continue with next tasks". Issue #2774 (gh issue view 2774) and DI-150 in projects/spaarke-ontology-platform-r1/notes/defer-issues.md. `src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Communication/Channels/EmailChannelSender.cs` (~265-290 on origin/master; both the `Me` and `Users[sender]` branches) reads `mailFolders/sentitems/messages` with `$filter=subject eq '...'` and `$orderby=sentDateTime desc`. Graph answers 400 for that combination (an $orderby property must also appear in the $filter, first), so after every send the Internet-Message-Id is lost for reply-thread matching and the archive. App Insights on dev shows `GET /v1.0/me/mailFolders/sentitems/messages` with resultCode 400 after sends.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE backend developer: .NET 10 BFF (Communication, Microsoft Graph SDK).</role>
  <goal>The Sent Items lookup returns the just-sent message (or a clean not-found) without a 400, in both branches, and the Internet-Message-Id is passed on as the code intends.</goal>
  <context>
    <background>Check Microsoft Graph's documented rule for $filter with $orderby on messages before choosing (Microsoft Learn: microsoft_docs_search "list messages filter orderby InefficientFilter"). Options: put sentDateTime first in the filter (sentDateTime ge {send time minus a margin} and subject eq ...) with the same $orderby, or drop $orderby and pick the newest client-side from a small $top. Keep the subject escaping (safeSubject) and the existing retry/delay behaviour for a message not yet in Sent Items. Keep what happens when nothing is found.</background>
  </context>
  <constraints>
    <constraint source="CLAUDE.md §6 gotcha 2026-11-24">Run the relevant --filter (for Signals code "FullyQualifiedName~Signals", which includes contract baselines; for Communication code "FullyQualifiedName~Communication"); update any baseline the change moves in the same PR.</constraint>
    <constraint source="root CLAUDE.md §10">BFF hygiene: publish-size delta vs fresh master (short paths, same zip tool, file counts) in the PR; no new HIGH CVE; no new package.</constraint>
    <constraint source="root CLAUDE.md §11">No new service, interface or DI registration unless the three questions are answered in the PR.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project CLAUDE.md §6">Filtered BFF tests only (never the unfiltered Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests); full ArchTests.</constraint>
    <constraint source="public repo">No environment GUIDs, user or contact ids, mailbox addresses or tenant names in code, tests, notes or the PR.</constraint>
  </constraints>
