  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">A test fails on origin/master: the lookup request built for both branches satisfies Graph's filter/orderby rule (asserted on the request the fake receives), and a found message's Internet-Message-Id is returned.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Not-found and Graph-error paths behave as before (no new exception escapes the send); subject escaping unchanged.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Build, filtered tests (Communication, EmailChannelSender) and full ArchTests pass; publish-size delta reported.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="false">(Not testable here) Main session confirms on dev after deploy that the sentitems GET no longer returns 400.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>
  <escalation>
    <trigger>The fix needs a new Graph permission, a change to the send itself, or a new package: STOP and report.</trigger>
  </escalation>
